mp itself does not always include `thread.id`, so the plugin does not rely on it for session identity.\n36: \n37: ## Session Management\n38: - Session ID source: Amp `thread.id`.\n39: - Session directory: `.entire/tmp/amp/`.\n40: - Bootstrap session file format: JSONL hook cache written by the external agent binary from plugin payloads.\n41: - Prepared session file format: exported Amp thread JSON, parsed as `AmpThread` from `internal/amp/types.go`.\n42: - Resume mechanism: `PLUGINS=all amp threads continue <thread-id>`.\n43: \n44: ## Transcript\n45: - Bootstrap location: `.entire/tmp/amp/<safe-thread-id>.json` before preparation. The file contains JSONL hook entries with at least `type`, `thread_id`, and optional prompt text.\n46: - Retrieval: `prepare-transcript --session-ref <path>` reads the bootstrap JSONL, extracts `thread_id`, runs `amp threads export <thread-id>`, and writes the exported JSON back to the same `session_ref` path.\n47: - Authoritative storage: after preparation, `session_ref` contains the exported Amp thread JSON byte-for-byte. This JSON is the session's native data and the input for all transcript operations.\n48: - Authoritative parser: `internal/amp/types.go` models the exported transcript as `AmpThread`, `ThreadMessage`, `ThreadContentBlock`, `ThreadToolRun`, and `ThreadUsage`.\n49: - User prompt extraction: `AmpThread.Messages[].Content[]` text blocks on `role: \"user\"` messages.\n50: - Assistant summary extraction: last non-empty text block on `role: \"assistant\"` messages.\n51: - Modified file extraction: `ThreadToolRun.TrackFiles`, tool input path fields (`path`, `filePath`, `filepath`, `file`, `absolutePath`, `paths`, `files`), and common tool result `absolutePath` fields.\n52: - Token usage extraction: `ThreadMessage.Usage` on exported messages.\n53: - Unprepared behavior: transcript analyzer, compact transcript, token calculation, and read-session operations require exported `AmpThread` JSON and return an error if called on the bo