xportThread(...)` to capture the freshly-completed turn; read latest model; return Type 3 event.\n- `modelFromExportedThread` becomes either removed or simplified into `latestModelFromSessionRef(sessionRef string) string` that only reads the file (no export side-effect). All explicit exports happen in the hook switch.\n\n### Tests\n\n`internal/amp/hooks_test.go`\n- Update `TestParseHookSessionStart`: still expects export (`assertExportedThread`).\n- Update `TestParseHookAgentStartWritesTranscript`:\n  - When no prepared file exists: assert agent.start triggers a fallback export (model = \"claude\").\n  - Add a sibling test where a prepared file is pre-written: assert agent.start does NOT call `ExportThread` (runner unchanged) and still reports the model.\n- Update `TestParseHookAgentEndWritesTranscript`: still expects export.\n- Existing `TestParseHookUsesSessionRefExportedThreadModel` already covers \"prepared file present → no re-export\" for session.start; keep it.\n\n`internal/amp/transcript_test.go`\n- Replace `TestPrepareTranscript`: pre-write a prepared `AmpThread` JSON at `path`; call `PrepareTranscript`; assert runner saw `threadID == \"T-123\"` and `outputPath == path`; assert file contents are the runner-written JSON.\n- Replace `TestPrepareTranscript_MissingThreadID` with `TestPrepareTranscript_UnpreparedFile`: write JSONL (or arbitrary non-AmpThread bytes); assert `PrepareTranscript` returns an error and `runner.threadID == \"\"`.\n- Replace `TestPrepareTranscript_RunnerError`: pre-write prepared JSON, runner returns error, assert error propagates.\n- Remove the JSONL-only `writeTestTranscript` helper (or repurpose for \"unprepared\" negative tests). Other tests that used `writeTestTranscript` for \"expect unprepared error\" can pass arbitrary JSONL bytes inline.\n\n### Docs\n\n`AGENT.md`\n- Section \"Session Management\": drop \"Bootstrap session file format\" line. Update to say `session_ref` is always the exported Amp thread JSON; the binary writes it on `session.start` and refreshes it on `agent.end`.\n- Section \"Transcript\": remove \"Bootstrap location\" and rewrite \"Retrieval\":\n  - \"The plugin fires `session.start` and `agent.end` hooks; the binary calls `amp threads export <thread-id>` and writes the result to `session_ref` on each. `prepare-transcript --session-ref <path>` re-runs the export using the thread ID stored in the existing prepared transcript.\"\n- Update \"Protocol Mapping\" rows:\n  - `parse-hook`: \"Map hook payloads to protocol events; export Amp thread on `session.start` and `agent.end`.\"\n  - `prepare-transcript`: \"Re-export the Amp thread using the thread ID from the current prepared transcript.\"\n- Remove the \"Gaps & Limitations\" bullet about the bootstrap JSONL cache.\n- Keep \"All transcript operations require the prepared `amp threads export` JSON\" bullet — still true.\n\n## Out of scope / non-changes\n- `compact.go`, `command_runner.go`, `agent.go`, `paths.go`, `types.go`: no changes.\n- The plugin TypeScript in `generatePlugin()` already sends `session.start`, `agent.start`, `agent.end` with `thread_id`. No change needed.\n- e2e harness and `external-agents-tests`: no protocol-surface changes, so no updates expected. Will run `mise run test` (or the agent's existing test task) to verify after the edits.\n\n## Verification\n- `go test ./...` in `agents/entire-agent-amp` after the refactor.\n- Spot-check that `TestInstallAndUninstallHooks`, `TestGeneratePlugin`, compact tests, and read-session tests still pass unchanged.",
