        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "## Summary\n\nRoot cause: `amp` is a Bun-compiled native binary. When invoked from inside an Amp plugin (which runs on Bun), the plugin's child-process environment leaks `BUN_BE_BUN=1` (and friends) through `entire` → `entire-agent-amp` → `amp`. With those vars set, a Bun-compiled binary re-enters Bun's script-runner mode and reads `argv[1]` (\"threads\") as a script name — producing `error: Script not found \"threads\"`.\n\nFix (`internal/amp/command_runner.go`):\n- New `ampEnv()` returns `os.Environ()` minus Bun bootstrap variables: `BUN_BE_BUN`, `BUN_INTERNAL_IPC_FD`, `BUN_INSPECT`, `BUN_INSPECT_NOTIFY`, `BUN_INSPECT_CONNECT_TO`, and anything matching `BUN_DEBUG_*`. User-meaningful vars like `BUN_INSTALL` are preserved.\n- `DefaultCommandRunner.ExportThread` now passes `append(ampEnv(), \"PLUGINS=all\")` as the env for the `amp` subprocess.\n- New unit tests `TestAmpEnvStripsBunVars` and `TestIsBunEnvVar` lock in the behavior.\n\nVerification:\n- `go test ./...` green.\n- Reproduced the original failure with `BUN_BE_BUN=1 amp threads export <id>` → `Script not found \"threads\"`.\n- Ran the agent binary's `parse-hook session.start` with the same `BUN_BE_BUN=1` leak: returns a valid Type 1 event and writes the prepared transcript, confirming the fix.",
